## portus.cookie — lectura y escritura de cookies HTTP.
##
## `parse_cookies` lee la cabecera `Cookie` de la petición (`a=1; b=2`) y
## `serialize_cookie` produce un valor de `Set-Cookie` con sus atributos.
##
## ## Ejemplo
## ```pengu
## calling context.set_header with "Set-Cookie", (calling portus.cookie.serialize_cookie with "sid", "abc", portus.cookie.session_options)
## ```
##
## ## Memoria
## `parse_cookies` devuelve un valor propio; libéralo con `free_cookies`.
## Los strings de `serialize_cookie` son propios.
import std.scrolls
import std.ward
import portus.text

## Una cookie de la petición.
rune CookiePair:
    ## Nombre tal cual vino.
    name as string
    ## Valor tal cual vino (sin decodificar).
    value as string

## Las cookies de una petición, en orden.
rune Cookies:
    ## Pares en el orden de la cabecera.
    pairs as list of CookiePair

## Atributos de una cookie de respuesta.
##
## `max_age` negativo omite `Max-Age`. `same_site` vacío omite `SameSite`;
## los valores habituales son `"Lax"`, `"Strict"` y `"None"`.
rune CookieOptions:
    ## Segundos de vida; negativo = cookie de sesión.
    max_age as int
    ## Ruta visible; vacío = `/` del navegador.
    path as string
    ## `HttpOnly` (no visible para JavaScript).
    http_only as bool
    ## `Secure` (solo HTTPS).
    secure as bool
    ## `SameSite`; vacío lo omite.
    same_site as string

## Opciones de una cookie de sesión razonable: `HttpOnly`, `SameSite=Lax`.
const SESSION_OPTIONS as CookieOptions is with max_age is -1, path is "/", http_only is true, secure is false, same_site is "Lax"

## Lee la cabecera `Cookie` completa.
##
## Ignora segmentos vacíos y espacios sobrantes. Un segmento sin `=` se guarda
## con valor `""`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un valor propio; libéralo con `free_cookies`.
weave parse_cookies with header as string into Cookies:
    var pairs as list of CookiePair is []
    if header.len == 0:
        return with pairs is pairs
    var parts as list of string is calling scrolls.split with header, ";"
    var i as int is 0
    while i < parts.len:
        var part as string is (parts at i)
        var trimmed as string is calling scrolls.trim with part
        if trimmed.len > 0:
            var eq as int is calling scrolls.index_of with trimmed, "="
            var name as string is ""
            var value as string is ""
            if eq < 0:
                set name is calling scrolls.substring with trimmed, 0, trimmed.len
            else:
                set name is calling scrolls.substring with trimmed, 0, eq
                set value is calling scrolls.substring with trimmed, eq + 1, trimmed.len
            calling pairs.push with with name is name, value is value
        banish trimmed
        set i is i + 1
    calling text.free_strings with parts
    return with pairs is pairs

## Valor de la cookie `name`, o `none`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Copia propia; libérala o pásala a `banish`.
weave cookie_get with cookies as Cookies, name as string into maybe string:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < cookies.pairs.len:
        var pair as CookiePair is (cookies.pairs at i)
        if (calling scrolls.compare with pair.name, name) == 0:
            return some (calling scrolls.substring with pair.value, 0, pair.value.len)
        set i is i + 1
    return maybe none

## `true` si la petición trae la cookie `name`.
weave cookie_has with cookies as Cookies, name as string into bool:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < cookies.pairs.len:
        var pair as CookiePair is (cookies.pairs at i)
        if (calling scrolls.compare with pair.name, name) == 0:
            return true
        set i is i + 1
    return false

## Libera las cookies y sus strings.
weave free_cookies with cookies as Cookies into void:
    var i as int is 0
    while i < cookies.pairs.len:
        var pair as CookiePair is (cookies.pairs at i)
        banish pair.name
        banish pair.value
        set i is i + 1
    banish cookies.pairs

## Construye el valor de `Set-Cookie` para `name=value`.
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un string propio.
weave serialize_cookie with name as string, value as string, options as CookieOptions into string:
    var out as string is "{name}={value}"
    if options.path.len > 0:
        set out is "{out}; Path={options.path}"
    if options.max_age >= 0:
        set out is "{out}; Max-Age={options.max_age}"
    if options.http_only:
        set out is "{out}; HttpOnly"
    if options.secure:
        set out is "{out}; Secure"
    if options.same_site.len > 0:
        set out is "{out}; SameSite={options.same_site}"
    return out

## Construye el `Set-Cookie` que borra una cookie (`Max-Age=0`).
##
## ## Memoria
## Devuelve un string propio.
weave clear_cookie with name as string, path as string into string:
    return "{name}=; Path={path}; Max-Age=0; HttpOnly"

test "parse_cookies lee pares y tolera espacios":
    var cookies as Cookies is calling parse_cookies with "sid=abc; theme=dark; bare"
    calling ward.assert_eq_int with cookies.pairs.len, 3
    let sid as maybe string is calling cookie_get with cookies, "sid"
    calling ward.assert_eq_string with (sid or else "?"), "abc"
    calling ward.assert_true with (calling cookie_has with cookies, "bare")
    calling free_cookies with cookies

test "serialize_cookie escribe atributos":
    var opts as CookieOptions is with max_age is 60, path is "/app", http_only is true, secure is true, same_site is "Strict"
    let text as string is calling serialize_cookie with "sid", "abc", opts
    calling ward.assert_eq_string with text, "sid=abc; Path=/app; Max-Age=60; HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Strict"
    banish text

test "clear_cookie pone Max-Age=0":
    let text as string is calling clear_cookie with "sid", "/"
    calling ward.assert_eq_string with text, "sid=; Path=/; Max-Age=0; HttpOnly"
    banish text
